---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import {fleetSystem} from '../../../data/small-fleet-system';
const checkout=fleetSystem.released&&fleetSystem.checkoutUrl?fleetSystem.checkoutUrl:null;
const groups=[['Schedule verified requirements','Keep date, mileage and dual triggers visible. Separate DATA ISSUE, overdue and due-soon status from the booking action.'],['Trust the mileage','Preserve accepted readings and review anomalies, corrections and stale data. Keep Unit ID stable across every record.'],['Control reported defects','Capture observations, owners, target dates and next actions without turning a symptom into an unsupported diagnosis.'],['Authorize and close repairs','Record approved scope and limits, changes, invoice evidence, recommendations, rule resets and downtime closure.'],['Review cost and disruption','Use defined fleet-paid categories and aligned mileage periods. Separate technical downtime, shop cycle and business impact.'],['Make evidence visible','Use monthly and quarterly review workspaces and a repair-versus-replace evidence pack. Management makes the decision.']];
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'WebPage',name:'Mercer Lane Small Fleet Maintenance System',description:'A connected Excel workbook and forms for small-fleet maintenance administration.',url:'https://mercerlanepress.com/tools/small-fleet-maintenance-system/'};
---
<BaseLayout title="Small Fleet Maintenance System | Excel Workbook & Forms" description="Connect vehicle records, verified maintenance rules, mileage, defects, repair approvals, service history, cost and downtime in a small-fleet Excel system." schema={schema}>
 <Breadcrumbs items={[{name:'Home',href:'/'},{name:'Tools',href:'/tools/'},{name:'Small Fleet Maintenance System'}]}/>
 <header class="wrap page-head"><p class="eyebrow">MERCER LANE PRESS · EXCEL SYSTEM + OPERATIONAL FORMS</p><h1>Small Fleet Maintenance System</h1><p class="lede">An Excel Control System for 3–50 Vehicles — Maintenance Scheduling, Defects, Repair Costs, Downtime and Vehicle Records</p><p>Give the next maintenance action a source, an owner and completion evidence. Bring the vehicle register, requirements, due work and repair administration into a connected working file.</p><div class="actions">{checkout?<a class="button" href={checkout} rel="noopener">Get the Small Fleet Maintenance System</a>:<a class="button" href="#availability">Check product availability</a>}<a class="button button-secondary" href="/tools/fleet-maintenance-due-calculator/">Try the free due calculator</a></div><p class="small" id="availability">{checkout?'One-time digital download. No product subscription. The book is sold separately.':'This product is being prepared for release. Checkout is not yet available. Try the free calculator while release testing is completed.'}</p></header>
 <section class="section section-tint"><div class="wrap"><h2>For the person keeping a small fleet organized</h2><p>Built for an owner, office manager, operations manager or fleet administrator handling cars, vans, pickups or light-duty vehicles across spreadsheets, email, paper and memory.</p><div class="grid-3">{groups.map(([heading,text])=><article class="card"><h3>{heading}</h3><p>{text}</p></article>)}</div></div></section>
 <section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow"><h2>What the digital package contains</h2><ul><li>Customer Blank XLSX with a finished Quick Start and connected operational tables.</li><li>Customer Demo XLSX using clearly fictional Northline-style records.</li><li>Practical Quick Start and User Guide PDF.</li><li>Editable Word and matching PDF operational forms: weekly exceptions, condition/defect report, authorization, service history, downtime, monthly and quarterly review, replacement evidence and 30-day implementation.</li><li>License and important use notes.</li></ul><p>Formulas are locked and entry cells are highlighted. No macros, add-ins, external workbook links or internet connection are needed for the core workbook.</p></div></section>
 <section class="section"><div class="wrap"><h2>Views from the working files</h2><p>Actual version 1.0 workbook renders. The dashboard uses fictional Northline records and a fixed 15 October 2026 date. Demo figures and intervals are illustrations, not recommendations or benchmarks. Desktop Excel acceptance testing remains open.</p><div class="preview-grid"><figure><a href="/images/small-fleet-system/dashboard.webp"><img src="/images/small-fleet-system/dashboard.webp" alt="Fictional demo dashboard showing seven active vehicles, overdue and due-soon requirements, audit issues, cost and downtime totals" width="2040" height="1318" loading="lazy" /></a><figcaption>Demo exception counts and period totals. Open the image for a larger view.</figcaption></figure><figure><a href="/images/small-fleet-system/quick-start.webp"><img src="/images/small-fleet-system/quick-start.webp" alt="Customer Blank Quick Start showing the five setup steps, input legend and weekly workflow" width="1488" height="1282" loading="lazy" /></a><figcaption>The blank workbook starts with a setup sequence. Open the image for a larger view.</figcaption></figure></div></div></section>
 <section class="section section-tint"><div class="wrap narrow"><h2>The book teaches the method. The digital system supplies the working files.</h2><p><a href="/books/the-small-fleet-maintenance-operating-manual/">The Small Fleet Maintenance Operating Manual</a> by Warren Holtby explains the operating process, source discipline and review decisions. This separate digital companion implements that process in workbooks and forms.</p><p><strong>The book is not included with the digital product.</strong></p><p><a class="button button-secondary" href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HM33JJL6">Read the book on Amazon</a></p></div></section>
 <section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow"><h2>Compatibility and practical limits</h2><p>The target is Microsoft Excel desktop. The workbook uses conventional functions including INDEX/MATCH, SUMIFS, COUNTIFS and EDATE. It uses no recent dynamic-array functions. Desktop Excel acceptance testing is still required before release; compatibility with a specific Excel version is not yet certified.</p><p>Prepared tables contain 60 vehicle rows, 300 rule/action rows and 500 mileage/service/reset rows. Use the prepared rows first. Expanding tables or sorting locked calculated tables requires temporarily unprotecting without a password, extending formulas and validation, checking the result and re-protecting. Filtering and routine entry remain available while protected.</p><p>Hours, event and condition triggers are documented manual-review fields. The free calculator and automatic workbook engine calculate date and mileage rules.</p><p>The system does not supply vehicle-specific intervals, diagnose faults, prevent breakdowns, guarantee savings or ensure compliance. It does not replace manufacturer information, qualified advice, legally required inspections, reporting or compliance systems.</p></div></section>
 <section class="section section-tint"><div class="wrap narrow"><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><details><summary>Is there a subscription?</summary><p>The planned product is a one-time digital download. Excel must be supplied separately. Price and purchase details will appear when payment configuration and release testing are complete.</p></details><details><summary>Can I use it without the book?</summary><p>The Quick Start and User Guide explain setup and routine use. The book provides the wider operating method and is sold separately.</p></details><details><summary>Are service intervals included?</summary><p>No. Enter requirements from the current appropriate verified source for your specific vehicle. All demo intervals and costs are fictional illustrations.</p></details><details><summary>Does it send reminders?</summary><p>No. Review the exception dashboard regularly. The workbook does not connect to calendars, send alerts or diagnose mechanical conditions.</p></details><details><summary>Can I try the calculation first?</summary><p>Use the completely free <a href="/tools/fleet-maintenance-due-calculator/">Fleet Maintenance Due Date &amp; Mileage Calculator</a> for one rule. No account or email is required.</p></details><details><summary>How will the digital download be delivered?</summary><p>When released, paid orders will use verified Stripe checkout and the site's private download delivery. The customer ZIP will not be stored in the public website repository.</p></details></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>.preview-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.5rem}.preview-grid figure{margin:0}.preview-grid img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid var(--line)}.preview-grid figcaption{font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:.7rem}@media(max-width:700px){.preview-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}.page-head h1{font-size:clamp(2.4rem,5vw,4rem);max-width:900px}.page-head p{max-width:900px}.small{font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:1rem}details{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:1rem 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}details p{margin-top:.8rem}</style>

